    "created_at": "2026-02-14T15:21:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-14T15:21:56Z",
    "body": "Hello, I am an end-user involved in the display of vertical text in Japanese.\r\n\r\nI think we need to add \"central\" to CanvasTextBaseline.\r\nIn CSS Writing Modes, the central baseline is used as the dominant baseline in vertical typographic mode when text-orientation is mixed or upright.\r\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-writing-modes-3/#text-baselines\r\n\r\nIn contrast, Canvas textBaseline=\"middle\" represents the midpoint between em-over and em-under (i.e. a geometric midpoint). This is a different concept from the typographic central baseline, so they are not interchangeable.\r\n\r\nIf this PR introduces writingMode=\"vertical\" and textOrientation, it should be possible to select \"central\" to keep alignment behavior consistent with CSS.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/3902056923/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
      "-1": 0,
